### Test Graylog Logging Integration
### This file contains test requests to verify GELF logging is working correctly
### Make sure 'graylog-enabled' profile is added to SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE before testing
### Example: SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=local,graylog-enabled

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8001
@correlationId = test-correlation-12345

### Test 1: Send SMS Verification (should generate logs with MDC fields)
### This will test:
### - Correlation ID in MDC (from X-Correlation-Id header)
### - Application logs (INFO, DEBUG, ERROR levels)
### - MDC fields: correlationId, phoneNumber (if added)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup/send-sms
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: {{correlationId}}
X-Device-Type: iOS

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

### Test 2: Send SMS with different device type (Android - Flash Call path)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup/send-sms
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-android-{{$timestamp}}
X-Device-Type: Android

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

### Test 3: Send SMS with Web device type
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup/send-sms
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-web-{{$timestamp}}
X-Device-Type: Web

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

### Test 4: Generate ERROR log (invalid phone number format)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup/send-sms
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-error-{{$timestamp}}
X-Device-Type: iOS

{
  "phoneNumber": "invalid-phone"
}

### Test 5: Generate WARNING log (rate limit exceeded - send multiple requests quickly)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup/send-sms
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-rate-limit-{{$timestamp}}
X-Device-Type: iOS

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

### Test 6: User login (different endpoint to test various log levels)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: test-login-{{$timestamp}}

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
  "password": "***REMOVED***"
}

### Test 7: Health check (should generate INFO logs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
X-Correlation-Id: test-health-{{$timestamp}}

### Expected Results in Graylog:
### 1. All logs should appear in Graylog with GELF format
### 2. Each log entry should include:
###    - correlationId (from MDC)
###    - service: "user-service"
###    - environment: "local" (or your active profile)
###    - facility: "user-service"
###    - source: file and line number (if include-source=true)
###    - level: INFO, DEBUG, WARN, ERROR
###    - message: the actual log message
###    - timestamp: log timestamp
### 3. Logs should be searchable by correlationId
### 4. Logs should be categorized by facility and service

### Verification Steps:
### 1. Enable Graylog: Set GRAYLOG_ENABLED=true environment variable
### 2. Start the application
### 3. Send test requests using the requests above
### 4. Check Graylog UI at your Graylog server
### 5. Search for logs with:
###    - correlationId: "test-correlation-12345"
###    - service: "user-service"
###    - facility: "user-service"
### 6. Verify MDC fields are included in log entries
### 7. Verify different log levels (INFO, DEBUG, WARN, ERROR) are captured

